# Copy to .env and adjust for docker compose. There is no secret-shaped
# configuration yet: no session, no OIDC, no CSRF and no form, so none of
# these need the envconf "_FILE" convention. The Umami URL and website id
# below are not secrets either. docker-compose.yaml reads this file itself;
# bin/website also runs with none of these set, since every one of them has
# a usable default.

# Address the public HTTP server listens on.
# ADDR=:8080

# Address govue's admin listener listens on: /healthz, /readyz and /metrics.
# ADMIN_ADDR=:8081

# debug, info, warn or error.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Comma separated CIDRs of the reverse proxies in front of the service, whose
# X-Forwarded-For header is believed. Empty trusts no header. Behind a proxy
# without this, page view counting sees only the proxy and counts nothing.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Server side page view counting through Umami, see docs/analytics.md.
# Off unless both are set; setting only one stops the start.
# Base URL of the Umami instance: https, or plain http for localhost or a
# name inside the cluster.
# UMAMI_URL=
# UUID of the website in Umami.
# UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
# Optional: bound of one post to Umami (1s to 30s, default 5s) and the number
# of views that may wait for a worker (1 to 10000, default 256).
# UMAMI_TIMEOUT=5s
# UMAMI_QUEUE_SIZE=256
